      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Effects that modify a creature\u2019s power and/or toughness, such as the effect of Titanic Growth, will apply to the creature no matter when they started to take effect. The same is true for any counters that change its power and/or toughness and effects that switch its power and toughness.",
      "oracle_id": "648aead4-dc0b-47bc-911c-8dcd2cfd32d3",
      "published_at": "2018-04-27",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the enchanted creature has an ability that grants abilities to other objects, Deep Freeze\u2019s effect will stop it from doing so. If the enchanted creature gains an ability after Deep Freeze resolves, it will keep that ability.",
      "oracle_id": "648aead4-dc0b-47bc-911c-8dcd2cfd32d3",
      "published_at": "2018-04-27",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Removing all +1/+1 counters from a creature affected by this ability or removing Sigarda's Summons from the battlefield will cause that creature to revert back to what it was. Notably, this may cause a creature to lose flying after it has been declared as an attacker but before blockers are declared. This may also result in a creature with damage already marked on it being destroyed if that damage is greater than the creature's toughness.",
